        'answer' => 'The car loan interest deduction lets eligible taxpayers deduct up to $10,000 a year of interest on a loan for a new, personal-use vehicle with final assembly in the United States, for tax years 2025 through 2028. It is available whether you itemize or take the standard deduction, and reported sources describe an income phase-out starting around $100,000 MAGI for single filers and $200,000 for joint filers.',
        'publish_at' => '2026-10-31 09:00',
