            [ 'What is the income limit for the car loan interest deduction?', 'Widely reported figures describe a phase-out starting around $100,000 of modified adjusted gross income for single filers and $200,000 for joint filers, reduced by $200 for every $1,000 over the threshold. The IRS page we could directly verify does not itself state these numbers, so confirm the exact thresholds in the final Schedule 1-A instructions before filing.' ],
