            [ 'Will my lender report the car loan interest to the IRS?', 'Generally, yes, starting with interest paid in the 2026 calendar year. IRS Publication 6127 describes a reporting requirement for businesses that receive $600 or more in qualified vehicle loan interest from an individual in a calendar year. For the 2025 tax year, you may need to request the interest figure directly from your lender.' ],
            [ 'Which vehicles qualify for the car loan interest deduction?', 'New cars, SUVs, vans, pickup trucks and motorcycles under 14,000 pounds gross vehicle weight rating generally qualify, as long as the final assembly happened in the United States and the loan is for personal, not business, use. Check the window sticker, the manufacturer\'s label, or decode the VIN at NHTSA\'s vpic.nhtsa.dot.gov to confirm a specific vehicle.' ],
